Fix printf-style format strings.

- HUGE_FORMAT: "%lld" assumed long long, but HUGE_TYPE is int64_t;
  use PRId64 from <inttypes.h> (-Wformat).
- s_zip_to_gmt: print the zip code bounded with snprintf() and an
  (int) cast wide enough for the 0-99999 domain, preserving leading
  zeros (-Wformat, -Wformat-truncation).
- dbgen_version, date_t_op(): bound the date/time/version strings with
  snprintf() and use %04hd/%02hhd with matching casts so the compiler
  can prove the buffers fit (-Wformat-overflow, -Wformat-truncation).
- print_delete(): the configured DELIMITER was passed as the format
  string; print it with "%s" (-Wformat-security -- a delimiter
  containing % previously invoked undefined behavior).

Generated data is unchanged: all rewritten formats produce the same
bytes for every value in their domain.

